      "id": 1,
      "text": "Felton was incorporated as a borough on May 8, 1899, after annexing parts of Chanceford, North Hopewell, and Windsor townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://feltonboroughpa.com/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s name honors Johannes Felton Ziegler, a financier who helped plan the railroad that first ran through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
